Step 16 — Jitter Measurement

For this project, we'll define measured jitter as the average absolute change between consecutive RTT measurements:

$$ J=\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{i=2}^{N}|RTT_i-RTT_{i-1}| $$

For example, if:

RTT = [20.5, 20.8, 20.6, 21.0]

the changes are:

0.3 ms
0.2 ms
0.4 ms

and jitter is their average.

This gives us another real measured QoS parameter for the later cost calculation.

